- Runtime capable of HTTPS requests.
- If using `scripts/api.ts`: TypeScript toolchain (or transpile to JS).

## Endpoints

### Auth Flow (1)
- `GET /assets/{assetToken}` — Authenticate and retrieve an asset.

### Data Read (8)
- `GET /HackerNews/API/activity/actors` — Get activity actors.
- `GET /HackerNews/API/branch_commits/{branch_commitHash}` — Get branch commit data by hash.
- `GET /HackerNews/API/commits/deferred_commit_contributors` — Retrieve deferred commit contributors.
- `GET /HackerNews/API/commits/deferred_commit_data/master` — Retrieve deferred commit data.
- `GET /HackerNews/API/hovercards/citation/sidebar_partial` — Fetch citation sidebar data.
- `GET /HackerNews/API/pulse-new/{pulse-newId}/weekly` — Get weekly pulse data.
- `GET /in/{inId}` — Retrieve information by ID.
- `GET /u/{uId}` — Get user profile data by ID.

### Data Write (4)
- `POST /_private/browser/stats` — Submit browser statistics.
- `POST /HackerNews/API/branches/deferred_metadata` — Submit deferred branch metadata.
- `POST /pull_request_review_decisions` — Submit pull request review decisions.
- `POST /v2/organizations/{organizationId}/environments/main/profiles` — Create or update an environment profile.

### Media (1)
- `GET /images/modules/site/lab/copilot/copilot_head.glb` — Download a 3D model asset.

### Core API (2)
- `GET /HackerNews/API/{APIId}` — Access core API functionality.
- `GET /HackerNews/API/{APIId}/master` — Access core API functionality on master branch.

## Quick Start

### OpenClaw (Unbrowse) workflow
- Authenticate in the browser first (no credentials are shipped with this skill).
- Capture fresh auth locally: run `unbrowse_capture` on an authenticated page for this domain.
- Execute via backend gate + client browser executor: `unbrowse_replay` with `executionMode="backend"`.

Example:
```text
unbrowse_replay { service: "github", executionMode: "backend", endpoint: "GET /HackerNews/API/activity/actors" }
```

